{#
  The "leave a comment" panel — the Twig counterpart of
  module/SionModel/view/sion-model/comments/create.phtml, which still renders it on
  production.

  Parameters:
    form         the SionModel\Form\CommentForm out of the laminas container, with its
                 `redirect` value and its action already set by the caller. The .phtml
                 supports a second mode where it builds the form itself from `entity`,
                 `entityId` and `kind` parameters; nothing in this application uses it
                 — all four show pages pass a prepared form — so it is not reproduced.
                 If a template ever needs it, build the form in the controller.
    form_action  where the POST goes: /comments/create/{entity}/{entity_id}/{kind}.

  The panel title is the `comment` element's own label ("Leave a comment") rather than
  a second literal, which is what the .phtml does — so the heading and the field label
  are one phrase in the catalogue, not two that can drift apart.

  `class="form"` rather than the usual `form-horizontal`: see
  App\Form\BootstrapFormRenderer::open(), which now takes the class rather than
  leaving the caller to str_replace it out of the rendered tag.

  The comment field is rendered as a bare element inside a plain `form-group` — no
  label, no help block — because the label is already the panel heading above it. The
  three below it are full rows.
#}
<div class="row"> <!-- comment create row -->
<div class="col-md-12">
<div class="panel panel-default" id="commentCreatePanel">
    <div class="panel-heading">
        <h3 class="panel-title"><i class="fa fa-paper-plane-o"></i> {{ translate(form.get('comment').getLabel()) }}</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-body">
    <div>
    	{{ form_open(form, form_action, 'form') }}
        <div class="form-group">
            {{ form_element(form.get('comment')) }}
        </div>
        {{- form_row(form.get('redirect')) }}
        {{- form_row(form.get('security')) }}
        {{- form_row(form.get('submit')) }}
        <!-- <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary"><i class="fa fa-reply"></i> Submit</button> -->
	{{ form_close() }}
    </div>
    </div> <!-- notes panel body -->
</div> <!-- comment create panel -->
</div> <!-- comment create column 12 -->
</div> <!-- comment create row -->
